CORE
defined-later.sh
--resolve-dynamic-sites --show-dynamic-sites
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^shell-command-name:defined-later.sh:8:1: .*: \{ "", "cat", "x" \}$
--
"b"
^warning: ignoring
--
Whether a function is defined is a constant at each instruction, so that
the call of g before its definition is known not to call it, and pager
does not get "b". The site itself may call g, as $pager may be g, with
the argument x and no second one.
